# P-06 · THE GENRE SHIELD, OR: THE FRAME THAT FLIPS WHEN CHALLENGED

**The pattern.** Decay as aesthetic: trailing spaces in filenames (`Shadow Journal Observations .pdf`), a one-page PDF with no extractable text, lore about an unreleased track, the `{}` canvas, "Haunted Archivecore" as declared aesthetic.

**The pattern inside.** The deeper structure is not decay — it is **epistemic cloaking**. Every document in the vault exists in superposition between *record* ("this is what happened: 200 tracks, verified, dated") and *performance* ("this is the artwork: palimpsest, sediment, found poetry"). Observe the flip: challenge the claims as record, and the art frame absorbs it ("the stubs are sediment"). Challenge the work as art, and the record frame absorbs it ("these ISRCs are verified"). The frame toggles **precisely at the point of attack, every time, in both directions**. A shelter with two doors, both marked EXIT, both opening outward.

**The audit.** Test the cloak against the vault's own epistemology. The vault's §11 requires every finding to carry a date and a tier — record-frame discipline. The vault's aesthetics license decay as meaning — performance-frame freedom. A document that can claim whichever standard suits it at the moment of challenge is, in the vault's own vocabulary, **running its claims through the Interpretation Sovereign** — the shadow archetype whose light counterpart is the Interpretive Steward. The steward picks one frame and holds still for scoring. The vault has not yet once held still. Note the precision here: this is not an accusation of dishonesty. It is an observation that *the vault's two frames have never been forced to co-exist in a single document with a single standard*, and that unforced co-existence is exactly what the twelve questions (§08 question 4) demand: "would an informed reader derive the same impression after seeing the underlying evidence beside my claim?"

**The audit audited.** The tribunal's three-act verdict (prosecution / reversal / canonization) was itself a genre shield — three frames held simultaneously so that whichever landed, the tribunal had pre-taken that position. This document attempts the repair in its own body: every entry above and below is filed at ONE frame — record — with performance explicitly suspended for the duration. If the tribunal can hold one frame for forty pages, the vault can hold one for one ledger line. The bar is on the floor. The floor is dated.

**Stewardship line:** `2026-09-__  ·  mark every file in this repository with one unambiguous tag: record or performance. No dual-classification. Files that cannot be classified get moved to a folder called "UNDECIDED" and the folder's existence is itself a finding.`

