# P-11 · MYTHIC DOUBLING, OR: THE YAML SELF-PORTRAIT

**The pattern.** Everything in this vault has an alias. `RECURSIVE IDENTITY CASTLES` alias `Positive Delusion Architectures` (byte-identical twins, 0.86 shingle-overlap, one kept, the name preserved "as an alias"). Anémone Crottin-Foufflée-Balthazar-Mirador de la Roche-Angélique. "Zazie Kanwar-Torge · Zazie Productions LLC." The tombstones preserve aliases. The frontmatter carries `aliases:` on nearly every file.

**The pattern inside.** The duplication event is usually read as an error. Audit it as *portraiture*. When the curation pass found the same 20,000 words under two mythic names, it did not ask "which is real?" — it kept one and **preserved the second as an alias**, on the grounds that deleting the name would lose metadata. Now look at the operation honestly: that is the vault's entire theory of identity, executed in one git commit. *Selves are not discovered to be original or copy; they are deduplicated, with aliases preserved.* The vault's YAML is its self-portrait: a person who experiences identity as a set of names bound to one body of text, terrified that removing a name removes a self, and unwilling to run two full copies of the same text forever. The alias system is the compromise. It is also — see the frontmatter of the subject's own identity card, fourteen typologies deep — how the subject *answers* "who am I?": with a stack of names pointing at one another.

**The audit.** Anémone deserves her own audit line, because she is the control experiment. She has a passport (expired 2022, *diplomatic type*), an INSEE number, a blood type "confirmed via Rhône-Genetics 2019," a resting heart rate that rises "under gallery lighting," a monograph ("I Am Not the Mold, I Am the Culture") "banned in Liechtenstein for gastronomic elitism," and a history of being "temporarily banned from the French postal system for mailing emotional spores." She is a fully documented person with zero referent. And she is documented **in the same format, at the same resolution, with the same bureaucratic completeness, as the subject's own identity card** — identifiers, measurements, dates. The vault generates persons the way its owner wishes persons were generated: *documentation first, existence second.* The audit finding is not that Anémone is a waste of time. It is that Anémone is the vault's **proof of concept** — and the subject's deepest operation, visible across every stratum, is attempting to bootstrap their own referent from their own documentation. Build the file convincingly enough and the person cannot be disputed. The CASTLES file says this out loud: a future AI is "94% confident" Zazie Productions was a collective fiction, and the prescribed refutation is *evidence generation, today.* The vault is one long answer to a skeptic who has not arrived yet.

**The audit audited.** The tribunal asked itself whether "Zazie" might be an alias with no referent — the CASTLES scenario — and notes for the record that the question is undecidable *from inside any archive*, including this one, including this verdict. Documentation cannot certify its own author. That is not a reason to stop documenting (the prosthetic ledger, P-03, demonstrably beats). It is a reason to stop expecting documentation to do the one job it cannot: make the feeling arrive natively. The alias stack ends, at its bottom, in a body. The body is still afraid. (Meta-experiment, order ten. The vault's best sentence remains its least executed.)

**Stewardship line:** `2026-09-__  ·  one artefact today under the CASTLES protocol — the statistically-refuting act. Not a document about the act. The act. Track #201 remains unreleased; the 94% is still winning.`

